    <h3>Programming Code Snippets</h3>
    <p>
      Review these typical scripting patterns to parse and format UTC and EST timestamps:
    </p>

    <h4>JavaScript Example (Node.js &amp; Browser)</h4>
    <pre style="background: var(--panel); padding: 1rem; border-radius: 6px; border: 1px solid var(--line); overflow-x: auto; color: var(--text); font-family: monospace;">{`// Store timestamp in UTC format
const currentUtc = new Date();
console.log("UTC ISO 8601 String:", currentUtc.toISOString());
// Output: "2026-07-15T08:19:00.000Z" (The 'Z' suffix stands for Zulu or UTC)

// Format the date for a client located in New York
const options = { timeZone: 'America/New_York', timeZoneName: 'short' };
console.log("Local Eastern Time:", currentUtc.toLocaleString('en-US', options));
// Output: "7/15/2026, 4:19:00 AM EDT" (Automatically handles summer daylight shift)`}</pre>

    <h4>Python Example</h4>
    <pre style="background: var(--panel); padding: 1rem; border-radius: 6px; border: 1px solid var(--line); overflow-x: auto; color: var(--text); font-family: monospace;">{`from datetime import datetime
import pytz

# Generate timezone-aware UTC datetime
utc_timezone = pytz.utc
utc_now = datetime.now(utc_timezone)
print("UTC Time:", utc_now.isoformat())
# Output: "2026-07-15T08:19:00.000000+00:00"

# Convert UTC timestamp to Eastern Time Zone
eastern_timezone = pytz.timezone('America/New_York')
eastern_now = utc_now.astimezone(eastern_timezone)
print("Eastern Time:", eastern_now.isoformat())
# Output: "2026-07-15T04:19:00.000000-04:00" (Correctly offsets to EDT UTC-4)`}</pre>

    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>API Responses</strong>: Modern APIs exchange date and time payloads formatted in ISO 8601 UTC notation (`2026-07-15T12:00:00Z`). Client applications parse the string and convert it to local EST/EDT depending on the client location.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Forex Trading</strong>: Foreign exchange trading operates 24 hours a day, synchronized to UTC. Brokers and traders track transaction settlement windows using UTC timestamps to prevent processing delays.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Remote Work Sync</strong>: Teams spanning multiple countries schedule international stand-ups using UTC. This prevents scheduling confusion when daylight saving rules change on different dates in the US and Europe.
      </li>
    </ul>
